{
 "_doc": "The Witcher rune system (docs/research/WORLD_LOCATIONS.md): numbered runes at treasure-map dig spots all over the map, in 14 rune tomes. Coordinates: ExploreOutlands' Witchers_Tmap_Locations.csv (fetched 2026-10-03; ids rarely change). Names and which tome holds each rune: read live from the public tomes at the Cambria Rune Library on 2026-10-03 (Hackworth). The library's tomes are locked down; a tome opens from within 2 tiles. Rows on a tome's main page are 'N - Place name'; the row's gem (button 100 + row) recalls with one of the tome's charges (shared, refilled by players), the detail page (200 + row) casts the spell (own mana + reagents). Find a rune's row by its name at use time: the order inside a tome may change. Rune 83 is in a tome but not in the coordinate table.",
